 "vocabulary": {
  "note": "Specs U01 to U13 (docs/ui-editor-gate-rules-round4.md). The step and assert names of the earlier files keep their meaning except where the rules file says a reading changes. The ones below are new or changed; the runner implements them after this file is locked. Nothing calls the page's own logic: values come from the DOM, computed style and layout.",
  "steps": {
   "tab": "Unchanged text of round 3, new reading (runner change #25): when the page has no element with role tab the step does nothing (there is no tab to click: every control is in one ribbon). When it has tabs (the earlier stubs) it behaves as before.",
   "clickBlank": "As before: a click on the empty part of the preview (deselects)."
  },
  "asserts": {
   "noTabs": "P5. No element of the whole page has role tablist, tab or tabpanel.",
   "ribbonGroups": "P5. [data-ribbon-panel] exists once and is inside [data-ribbon]; its [data-ribbon-group] elements, in document order, are the keys of `groups` in that order, each with role group and aria-label equal to the name; with visibleAll every group is rendered (a client rect) and inside the window; every control named is a button, input or select with that accessible name (aria-label, else its text) inside its group; every button, input and select inside [data-ribbon] lies inside a [data-ribbon-group], except those named in `exempt`, which must lie inside [data-ribbon-strip]; no accessible name occurs twice inside [data-ribbon].",
   "ribbonSpread": "P1. Bands are the distinct tops (rounded to 6 px) of the visible [data-ribbon-group] elements. `maxBands` is the most allowed (1 means exactly one). The ribbon's inner edges are the box of [data-ribbon-panel] less its border and padding. For every band: the first group's left edge is within edgeTol of the inner left edge and the last group's right edge within edgeTol of the inner right edge; the gaps between neighbouring group boxes differ by at most gapTol; the gaps between the nearest controls of neighbouring groups (the right-most control edge of one to the left-most control edge of the next) differ by at most controlGapTol (my definition of \"extra width is distributed evenly\"); every group except the last of its band has a visible thin separator (a border of at least 1 px, not transparent, on one side); no group is split (every control box of a group lies inside the group's box within 0.5 px), none is clipped (inside the panel's box within 0.5 px), and [data-ribbon-panel] and the page do not scroll sideways (scrollWidth <= clientWidth + 1).",
   "ribbonLabels": "P5. Every visible button, input (not hidden) and select of [data-ribbon-panel] and [data-ribbon-strip], except the names in `exempt` (the Link checkbox, whose label sits beside it), has a label: either its own visible text of at least three letters (Sides, Move up, Move down, Grid, Snap, and the quick-bar style words), or the nearest visible [data-ctl-label] element whose box is within `reach` px of the control's box (distance between the two rectangles) and overlaps it horizontally. Each [data-ctl-label] has a computed font size between minFont and maxFont (inclusive, 0.01), text of 1 to maxWords words, sentence case (first letter upper case, not all capitals unless one letter, which is forbidden anyway), a computed colour equal to the page's `colour` custom property resolved by the runner, and is not any of `forbidden` (exact, case-insensitive) and is not a single character. The label contains the control's accessible name (case-insensitive) or equals the `table` entry for the name (after removing a leading Decrease, Increase or Pick, and the trailing ' sides' only through the table entry). `captions`: the labels of those buttons equal the given words exactly. `words`: those controls' own visible text equals the given text exactly.",
   "tooltips": "P5. Every visible button, input (not hidden), select and the Link checkbox of [data-ribbon] has a non-empty title of at least minWords words, whose first word (letters only) is one of `verbs` (case-sensitive) and which is not equal to the control's accessible name.",
   "sameAs": "As round 3 (P1 or P5). The measure named by `what` equals the remembered number within tol.",
   "controlSizes": "As round 3 (P1): the controls of the visible [data-ribbon-panel] (now the only panel) are 26 to 28 px high (+- tol) except the largeNames (54 to 62 and at least 40 wide); every visible group has a [data-group-label] of labelSize under its controls. The `tab` parameter has no meaning in round 4 and is ignored.",
   "fieldsFit": "P1. For the selected element, every visible text input of [data-ribbon-panel] has scrollWidth <= clientWidth; every visible select shows its selected option's whole text: the text measured with the select's own font on a canvas, plus the select's horizontal padding and border and 22 px for the arrow, is at most its clientWidth + 0.5 (my definition: a select does not report its overflow). The selected element's label is recorded; with minDistinct the number of distinct labels recorded so far in the spec must be at least that.",
   "fontShows": "P5. The Font family select's selected option text equals `expect` exactly; its title contains `stackContains` (the full stack in the tooltip); its option texts are exactly `options`, in order, and none contains a comma.",
   "fillShows": "P5. The Background text input's value equals `expect` when compared without case, and its scrollWidth <= clientWidth.",
   "statusLine": "P1. The element with role status named Edit result: its box is at most maxHeight tall; it is one line (its text box, measured by a Range, has one distinct line top; no child is taller than 1.6 times the computed line height); its top is not above the bottom of [data-ribbon] (0.5 px) and at most gapMax px below it; [data-stage-area] starts at or below its bottom (0.5 px); with messageShown its text is not empty; its height is stored under `key`, and with sameHeightAs it equals the stored height of that key within 1 px (reserved space).",
   "tabOrder": "P5. With an element selected, focus is put on the first visible enabled control of [data-ribbon] in visual order, then Tab is pressed up to `max` times until focus leaves [data-ribbon]. The sequence of focused controls equals the list of all visible, enabled buttons, inputs (not hidden) and selects of [data-ribbon] (the strip's checkbox included) in visual order: strip first, then band by band, in each band group by group from left to right, in each group row by row (control tops within 12 px are one row), left to right. Each focused control shows a focus indicator: an outline of at least 1 px and a style other than none, or a box-shadow other than none, and different from the same control unfocused. (my definition of visual order and indicator)",
   "enabledOnly": "P5. With a document open, the controls of [data-ribbon] named in `names` (Grid, Snap, Grid spacing) are enabled, and every other visible button, input and select of [data-ribbon] (the Link checkbox too) is disabled.",
   "quickBarWords": "P5. Read in the group Editor controls: for each of `words`, the button whose name matches (Review unlinked matches Review unlinked (N)) is visible and its visible text (innerText, trimmed) contains the text; for each of `iconOnly`, the button's visible text is empty and its aria-label and title are not empty.",
   "limitsHas": "P5. The list items under the heading Limits contain one whose text, with whitespace normalised, contains `sentence`. U13 is scored only when the sentence was verified in Step 1; otherwise the runner is given --u13-na and the spec reads NOT APPLICABLE when the sentence is absent (and FAILs if it is present).",
   "ribbonWraps": "As round 3: at least minRows distinct group tops (6 px).",
   "ribbonHit": "As round 2/3.",
   "noClipped": "As round 3 (no tab elements now)."
  }
 },
